# 1. Executive Summary

Aegis Resolve AI is an Explainable Multi-Agent Dispute Resolution Platform designed to modernize payment dispute handling through cloud-native architecture, intelligent orchestration, and transparent AI decision making.

Unlike conventional dispute systems that rely on manual investigation or opaque AI predictions, Aegis Resolve AI introduces a Digital Arbitration Court where specialized AI agents collaboratively analyze evidence, validate policies, evaluate fairness, and produce explainable verdicts with human oversight.

The architecture emphasizes:

- Explainable AI
- Multi-Agent Collaboration
- Evidence Trust Graph
- Event-Driven Processing
- Enterprise Security
- Human-in-the-Loop
- Cloud-Native Scalability

---

# 2. Architecture Principles

| Principle | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| Explainable by Design | Every AI decision is supported by evidence and reasoning. |
| Human-Centered | Human analysts review low-confidence decisions. |
| Event Driven | Services communicate asynchronously through Kafka. |
| Security First | Zero Trust architecture with RBAC and encryption. |
| Cloud Native | Containerized microservices deployed on Kubernetes. |
| AI Governance | Fairness, confidence, and compliance checks are mandatory. |
| Scalability | Every layer supports horizontal scaling. |

